---
description: Follow glinter when writing git commit messages
alwaysApply: true
---

When writing, amending, or squashing git commits, follow
`.cursor/skills/glinter/SKILL.md` or `~/.cursor/skills/glinter/SKILL.md`.

- Imperative subject, ≤50 characters preferred, hard cap 72
- Capitalize the subject; no trailing period
- Blank line before the body; wrap the body at 72
- Simple prose: no adverbs, passive voice, qualifiers, or weasel words
- No Conventional Commits prefixes (`feat:`, `fix:`)
- If `bin/glinter` exists, run it on the message and fix every finding
- Do not use `--no-verify` to skip a commit-msg hook
